
According to a new report from Intel Market Research, the global Cloud Electrification Retail Technology Market was valued at USD 3.45 billion in 2025 and is projected to reach USD 6.78 billion by 2034, growing at a robust CAGR of 7.1% during the forecast period (2026–2034). This growth is propelled by retailers’ accelerating sustainability agendas, the expanding demand for on‑site electric‑vehicle (EV) charging, and the rapid maturation of cloud‑enabled energy‑management platforms that combine real‑time analytics, AI‑driven load balancing, and subscription‑based energy‑as‑a‑service models.
What is Cloud Electrification Retail Technology?
Cloud Electrification Retail Technology integrates cloud‑based computing resources with EV‑charging hardware, intelligent energy‑distribution systems, and modern point‑of‑sale (POS) infrastructure. The solution stack enables retailers to monitor power consumption across dozens or hundreds of locations, dynamically allocate electricity to high‑demand assets, and provide customers with seamless, pay‑per‑use EV‑charging experiences-all while reducing overall energy costs and supporting corporate ESG commitments.
